  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A cssMode slider now has Swiper's mousewheel module switched on unless Mousewheel is set. Swiper 14 leaves the wheel of a cssMode slider to the browser only while that module is on; with it off, its init hook puts a listener on the wrapper that cancels every wheel event and steps one page instead, so neither the slider nor a native scroller inside it could be scrolled with a wheel or a trackpad, and a host had to pass Mousewheel = new() on every cssMode slider to get that back. Any Mousewheel you set still wins, including Mousewheel = false. Only a CssMode set directly on the options is covered: for one that arrives through a breakpoint or the css-mode attribute, set Mousewheel yourself. A programmatic cssMode move now also hands the slider back to a wheel turned over it mid-move, as it already did for a drag: with the module on the wheel never reaches Swiper's slideTo, so the move had nothing to hear it by and kept overwriting the scroll position every frame. A wheel over content that Swiper itself ignores (the swiper-no-mousewheel class, or a custom NoMousewheelClass) leaves the move running, and the wheel listener is released together with Swiper's own instance when its container leaves the DOM. Behaviour change, no API change. Same vendored Swiper 14.4.0 bundle.",
